---

<DocsLayout
  title="Markly"
  description="Save and organize bookmarks, build pin collections, create personal dictionaries, track activity, and manage syncing, imports, exports, and reports with Markly."
>
  <main class="markly-page">
    <section class="hero">
      <div class="hero-copy reveal">
        <p class="eyebrow">Meet Markly</p>

        <h1>Save what matters, organize it your way, and keep it easy to find again.</h1>

        <p class="hero-text">
          Markly is a bookmark and reference organizer built for the things you
          want to keep, revisit, sort, and understand later. Save links into folders,
          favorite or pin important bookmarks, build quick-access collections,
          create personal dictionaries with detailed word entries, review recent
          activity, and manage syncing, imports, exports, and support from one
          connected place.
        </p>

        <div class="hero-actions" aria-label="Markly links">
          <a class="primary-button raised-button" href="#features">
            Explore Features
          </a>

          <a class="secondary-button raised-button" href="/contact">
            Contact Support
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="hero-showcase reveal reveal-delay">
        <div class="showcase-card main-card">
          <h4>Bookmarks, collections, and words stay connected.</h4>

          <div class="progress-line">
            <span></span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="floating-card floating-card-one">
          <span>Library</span>
          <strong>Folders, favorites, and saved links</strong>
        </div>

        <div class="floating-card floating-card-two">
          <span>Dictionary</span>
          <strong>Definitions, sources, tags, and notes</strong>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <GradientDivider />

    <section class="intro-section reveal">
      <p class="eyebrow">One Connected Library</p>

      <h2>Your saved links, collections, words, and activity should not feel like separate systems.</h2>

      <p>
        Markly connects bookmark folders, pinned collections, personal dictionaries,
        recent activity, account syncing, and import/export tools into one organized
        library. Instead of scattering saved information across unrelated places,
        you can keep the things you want to revisit structured around how you
        actually use them.
      </p>
    </section>

