    <section
      class="feature-grid"
      id="features"
      aria-label="Markly features"
    >
      <article class="feature-card wide reveal">
        <p class="card-kicker">Bookmark Library</p>

        <h3>Build a bookmark library that stays organized beyond the moment you save something</h3>

        <p>
          Create and reorder folders, keep a permanent Inbox, add and edit bookmarks,
          search folders, move saved links between folders, favorite important items,
          and open detailed bookmark views when you need the full context. Markly
          also tracks folder, bookmark, and favorite counts so the shape of your
          library stays visible.
        </p>

        <div class="chip-row">
          <span>Folders</span>
          <span>Inbox</span>
          <span>Favorites</span>
          <span>Search</span>
          <span>Reordering</span>
          <span>Bookmark Details</span>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="feature-card reveal">
        <p class="card-kicker">Pins</p>

        <h3>Keep your most useful saved links one step closer</h3>

        <p>
          Pin bookmarks from your library, search across pinned items, and group
          them into custom collections with names, icons, notes, and their own
          detail views. Collections give frequently used bookmark groups a faster
          home without changing the folder structure of the main library.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="feature-card reveal">
        <p class="card-kicker">Personal Dictionaries</p>

        <h3>Build word collections with more depth than a simple definition list</h3>

        <p>
          Create multiple dictionaries, search them, edit or delete them, and open
          each one into its own word collection. Dictionary entries can carry the
          word itself, part of speech, source name and link, pronunciation, IPA,
          synonyms, antonyms, multiple definitions, example sentences, etymology,
          related words, tags, and usage notes.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="feature-card reveal">
        <p class="card-kicker">Activity</p>

        <h3>See how your saved library has been growing and changing</h3>

        <p>
          Markly's Activity area brings together recent bookmark saves, available
          folders, and pin collections in a time-ordered feed, with overview counts
          for folders, bookmarks, and collections. It gives you a simple history of
          the information you have been organizing inside the app.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="feature-card reveal">
        <p class="card-kicker">Sharing & Import</p>

        <h3>Bring bookmarks into Markly from outside the app and keep shared folders ready</h3>

        <p>
          Markly includes share-extension support for incoming bookmarks, a shared
          Inbox flow, shared-folder export data, and tools for importing bookmark
          data from other sources. New shared items can be picked up by the library
          and folded into the same folder system you already use.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="feature-card wide reveal">
        <p class="card-kicker">Cloud & Data</p>

        <h3>Keep control over syncing, backups, and moving your bookmark data</h3>

        <p>
          Markly includes account sign-in, Cloud Sync management, bookmark export,
          bookmark import, and shared-folder refresh tools. The data side of the
          app is kept alongside the library itself so saving information does not
          mean giving up control over how it moves between devices or sources.
        </p>

        <div class="reader-preview">
          <div class="reader-preview-top">
            <span>Data Tools</span>
            <strong>Connected</strong>
          </div>

          <div class="reader-bar">
            <span></span>
          </div>

          <div class="reader-meta">
            <span>Cloud Sync</span>
            <span>Import</span>
            <span>Export</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>
    </section>

    <section class="spotlight reveal">
      <div class="spotlight-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">Organize for Retrieval</p>

        <h2>Saving something is only useful if finding it again stays easy</h2>

        <p>
          Markly is built around retrieval as much as collection. Folder search,
          pinned collections, favorites, detailed bookmark records, dictionary
          search, tags, activity history, and import/export tools all give saved
          information more than one path back to you.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="share-demo" aria-label="Markly organization preview">
        <span class="share-pill">Find It Again</span>

        <h4>Give saved information more than one way back.</h4>

        <div class="share-row">
          <span>Folders</span>
          <strong>Organize the main bookmark library</strong>
        </div>

        <div class="share-row">
          <span>Pins</span>
          <strong>Create faster access collections</strong>
        </div>

        <div class="share-row">
          <span>Dictionary</span>
          <strong>Build searchable word references</strong>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="details-section reveal">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">Everything Else</p>

        <h2>Open each part of the Markly experience</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="details-list">
        <details open>
          <summary>
            <span>
              <b>Bookmark Folders & Inbox</b>
              <small>Organize links into a reorderable folder system with a stable home for new saves</small>
            </span>
          </summary>

          <p>
            Markly's Library centers on folders, including a protected Inbox that
            receives new shared items and keeps orphaned bookmarks from disappearing.
            Folders can be created, renamed, reordered, searched, and deleted, with
            their bookmarks moved safely back into Inbox when needed.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>
            <span>
              <b>Bookmark Details & Web Viewing</b>
              <small>Keep metadata around each saved link and open it without losing context</small>
            </span>
          </summary>

          <p>
            Individual bookmarks have dedicated detail views, editable metadata,
            tags, favorites and pinning behavior, plus an in-app web view for opening
            saved links. Bookmark cards keep titles, URLs, descriptions, icons, and
            tags visible before you even open the full detail screen.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>
            <span>
              <b>Pin Collections</b>
              <small>Create quick-access groups without changing your main folder organization</small>
            </span>
          </summary>

          <p>
            Pin collections can be created with a custom name and icon, opened in
            their own collection view, and used to group pinned bookmarks separately
            from the Library. This gives frequently used groups a faster access path
            while preserving the main bookmark structure.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>
            <span>
              <b>Rich Dictionary Entries</b>
              <small>Capture words with source, pronunciation, relationships, examples, and usage context</small>
            </span>
          </summary>

          <p>
            Dictionary words are designed for deeper reference, supporting source
            attribution and links, pronunciation and IPA, synonyms and antonyms,
            multiple definitions, example sentences, origin and etymology, related
            words, tags, and usage notes instead of reducing each word to one line.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>
            <span>
              <b>Share Extension & Shared Inbox</b>
              <small>Capture bookmarks from elsewhere and bring them into the same library</small>
            </span>
          </summary>

          <p>
            Shared bookmark payloads can be passed into Markly from the share
            extension and imported into the app's bookmark system. Shared folder
            data is maintained so external saving flows can stay aligned with the
            folders already available inside Markly.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>
            <span>
              <b>Activity Overview</b>
              <small>See recent saves and organization activity alongside library totals</small>
            </span>
          </summary>

          <p>
            The Activity page combines recent bookmark, folder, and collection
            events into a chronological feed and pairs that history with overview
            counts for folders, bookmarks, and collections so recent changes are
            easier to understand at a glance.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>
            <span>
              <b>Account, Sync, Import, Export & Reports</b>
              <small>Manage data movement, account state, and support without leaving Markly</small>
            </span>
          </summary>

          <p>
            Settings includes Sign in with Apple, Cloud Sync, bookmark export,
            bookmark import, shared-folder refresh, bug reports, feature requests,
            beta feedback, submitted report history, Privacy Policy, and Terms of
            Service, keeping account, data, and support tools in one place.
          </p>
        </details>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="community-banner reveal">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Built Around the Things You Keep</p>

        <h2>Saved information becomes more valuable when its structure survives after the moment you save it.</h2>

        <p>
          Markly is built around the full life of saved information: capturing a
          link, placing it somewhere meaningful, pinning what matters most, adding
          context, building reference collections, finding things again, moving
          data between sources, and seeing how your library changes over time.
        </p>
      </div>

      <a class="primary-button raised-button" href="https://discord.gg/SaZJKF3d9U">
        Join the Community
      </a>
    </section>

    <section class="cta-section reveal">
      <p class="eyebrow">Explore Markly</p>

      <h2>Keep the links, words, and references you care about organized and easy to return to.</h2>

      <p>
        Learn more about Markly, report a problem, share an idea, or reach out
        directly through Voxiverse Support.
      </p>

      <div class="cta-grid">
        <a
          href="https://github.com/asteriasmoons/Markly/issues/1"
          class="cta-card"
        >
          <span class="cta-kicker">Report an Issue</span>

          <h2>Markly Bug Reports</h2>

          <span class="cta-button">Open Reports</span>
        </a>

        <a href="/github" class="cta-card">
          <span class="cta-kicker">Ideas & Discussions</span>

          <h2>Voxiverse on GitHub</h2>

          <span class="cta-button">Open GitHub</span>
        </a>

        <a href="/contact" class="cta-card">
          <span class="cta-kicker">Need Help?</span>

          <h2>Contact Support</h2>

          <span class="cta-button">Get Support</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</DocsLayout>

<script>
  const revealItems = document.querySelectorAll(".reveal");

  const revealObserver = new IntersectionObserver(
    (entries) => {
      entries.forEach((entry) => {
        if (entry.isIntersecting) {
          entry.target.classList.add("is-visible");
          revealObserver.unobserve(entry.target);
        }
      });
    },
    { threshold: 0.12 }
  );

  revealItems.forEach((item) => revealObserver.observe(item));

  document
    .querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>("[data-markly-gallery]")
    .forEach((gallery) => {
      const track =
        gallery.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-gallery-track]");

      const slides = Array.from(
        gallery.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>(".gallery-slide")
      );

      const previousButton =
        gallery.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>(
          "[data-gallery-previous]"
        );

      const nextButton =
        gallery.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>(
          "[data-gallery-next]"
        );

      const count =
        gallery.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-gallery-count]");

      const progress =
        gallery.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-gallery-progress]");

      if (
        !track ||
        !slides.length ||
        !previousButton ||
        !nextButton
      ) {
        return;
      }

      let currentIndex = 0;
      let autoplay: number | undefined;
      let dragStartX = 0;

      const updateGallery = () => {
        track.style.transform =
          `translateX(-${currentIndex * 100}%)`;

        slides.forEach((slide, index) => {
          slide.classList.toggle(
            "is-active",
            index === currentIndex
          );
        });

        if (count) {
          count.textContent =
            `${currentIndex + 1} / ${slides.length}`;
        }

        if (progress) {
          progress.style.width =
            `${((currentIndex + 1) / slides.length) * 100}%`;
        }
      };

      const showSlide = (index: number) => {
        currentIndex =
          (index + slides.length) % slides.length;

        updateGallery();
      };

      const startAutoplay = () => {
        window.clearInterval(autoplay);

        autoplay = window.setInterval(
          () => showSlide(currentIndex + 1),
          4200
        );
      };

      const stopAutoplay = () => {
        window.clearInterval(autoplay);
      };

      nextButton.addEventListener("click", () => {
        showSlide(currentIndex + 1);
        startAutoplay();
      });

      previousButton.addEventListener("click", () => {
        showSlide(currentIndex - 1);
        startAutoplay();
      });

      gallery.addEventListener("pointerdown", (event) => {
        dragStartX = event.clientX;
        stopAutoplay();
      });

      gallery.addEventListener("pointerup", (event) => {
        const deltaX = event.clientX - dragStartX;

        if (Math.abs(deltaX) > 40) {
          showSlide(
            currentIndex + (deltaX < 0 ? 1 : -1)
          );
        }

        startAutoplay();
      });

      gallery.addEventListener(
        "mouseenter",
        stopAutoplay
      );

      gallery.addEventListener(
        "mouseleave",
        startAutoplay
      );

      gallery.addEventListener(
        "focusin",
        stopAutoplay
      );

      gallery.addEventListener(
        "focusout",
        startAutoplay
      );

      window.addEventListener(
        "resize",
        updateGallery
      );

      updateGallery();
      startAutoplay();
    });
</script>

<style>
  .markly-page {
    position: relative;
    width: 100%;
    padding: 1rem 0 5rem;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .hero {
    position: relative;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns:
      minmax(0, 1.2fr)
      minmax(310px, 0.8fr);
    align-items: center;
    gap: 3rem;
    min-height: 620px;
    padding: 4rem 0;
  }

  .hero-copy,
  .hero-showcase {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 2;
  }

  .hero h1 {
    max-width: 860px;
    margin: 0 0 1.25rem;
    font-size: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 6.5rem);
    line-height: 0.96;
    letter-spacing: -0.055em;
  }

  .eyebrow,
  .card-kicker,
  .mini-label {
    margin: 0 0 0.85rem;
    font-size: 0.76rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .hero-text,
  .intro-section p,
  .spotlight p,
  .community-banner p,
  .cta-section > p {
    max-width: 760px;
    font-size: 1.06rem;
  }

  .hero-actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.85rem;
    margin-top: 2rem;
  }

  .primary-button,
  .secondary-button {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    min-height: 50px;
    padding: 0.9rem 1.3rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 999px;
    color: var(--color-bg);
    text-decoration: none;
    transition:
      transform 0.2s ease,
      border-color 0.2s ease;
  }

  .primary-button {
    background: var(--accent-periwinkle);
  }

  .secondary-button {
    background: var(--surface-raised) !important;
    color: var(--color-text) !important;
  }

  .primary-button:hover,
  .secondary-button:hover {
    transform: translateY(-3px);
    border-color: var(--accent-periwinkle);
  }

  .hero-showcase {
    min-height: 410px;
  }

  .showcase-card,
  .floating-card,
  .feature-card,
  .share-demo,
  .details-list details,
  .community-banner,
  .cta-card {
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    background: var(--surface-standard);
    box-shadow: var(--glass-shadow-soft);
  }

  .main-card {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 55px 20px 55px 30px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: center;
    padding: 2rem;
    border-radius: 30px;
    transform: rotate(2deg);
  }

  .main-card h4 {
    max-width: 420px;
    margin: 0;
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3.6rem);
    line-height: 1.05;
  }

  .progress-line {
    height: 10px;
    margin: 1.75rem 0;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--surface-raised);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .progress-line span {
    display: block;
    width: 72%;
    height: 100%;
    border-radius: inherit;
    background: var(--accent-periwinkle);
    animation: pulse-width 3s ease-in-out infinite;
  }

  .showcase-stats {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 1rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .showcase-stats b {
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .floating-card {
    position: absolute;
    z-index: 3;
    padding: 1rem 1.15rem;
    border-radius: 18px;
    animation: float 5s ease-in-out infinite;
  }

